# Markdown Studio

When a Markdown file is meant to become a PDF or printed document:

1. Call the `get_markdown_guide` tool from the `markdown-studio` MCP server (or read the `markdown-studio` skill) before writing.
2. Structure: one `#` title, `##` sections, no skipped heading levels, tables for structured data, `> [!NOTE]`-style callouts, languages on every code fence, `\pagebreak` on its own line for manual breaks.
3. Do not hand-write a table of contents or heading numbers — pass `settings.toc` / `settings.headingNumbers` instead.
4. Avoid LaTeX math, HTML layout tags and YAML front-matter: they do not render.
5. Run `analyze_markdown` and fix all warnings, then `render_pdf` with settings from the closest template (`list_templates`).
6. As soon as `render_pdf` returns, save the PDF and open it automatically in a canvas (a `.canvas.tsx` that embeds the base64 PDF in an `<iframe src="data:application/pdf;base64,…">`), so it appears beside the chat. Do not open it in Preview, a browser or any external app, and do not ask first.
